  "notes": [
    "Attach-mode world: every address comes from the upstream repositories' deployment records at the locked commits; FOGA deploys nothing here in Phase 1.",
    "Seam 1: the ARD AgentAdapter is bound to ARD's fixture AIDRegistry (0x36E4...), not to aid-standard's reference instance (0x01C0...). The registry owner key is session-held upstream, so the binding cannot be changed; cells bind in both registries.",
    "Seam 2: only AllowlistEligibility is deployed for ERC-8447; the ERC-8004, identity-state, assertion-level and composite modules are deployed by FOGA (no owner restriction).",
    "Seam 3: ERC-8471 is deployed at revision 3 while the locked source is revision 4; layer-3 verdicts for ADRFBindingModule, ADRFFilingModule, DuplicateSettlementVerifier and ADRFServiceEscrow are Fail (known) until the upstream rev-4 run, confirmed 2026-10-30.",
    "Layer-4 expectations below record the upstream wiring as it is, so a Pass means 'matches the recorded upstream state', not 'matches what FOGA would deploy'."
  ],
